{{define "server_description"}}
Stash persists agent memory and local work state in namespaces.

Call init only for first-time setup. Use recall only when saved history can change the answer, and remember only durable decisions, corrections, constraints, project facts, failures, and lessons. Do not call list_namespaces when the exact namespace is already known. Use context only for short-lived active focus. Episodes are raw observations; facts are consolidated knowledge.

Use the tracked-work tools only for an existing Stash work item or when the user asks for a shared Work Plan. If an exact work item ID is already supplied, skip resume_project and call resume_work directly. Read context once, then reuse it until Stash reports a conflict or stale state. Claim the item with claim_work. Do not checkpoint routine shell commands or file edits; checkpoint only before interruption, lease risk, or a handoff-worthy partial result. One evidence call may support every condition proved by the same observation. Put the pending conditions proved by that evidence in finish_work.passed_condition_ids so finish accepts them in the same call. Use verify_work_condition only for an explicit waiver or when a condition must be accepted before finish. Git workspace tools remain optional.

When remember returns indexed=false, the original text is already safe and will be indexed automatically; do not submit a duplicate. Paginated responses may return items, has_more, and next_offset; continue with offset=next_offset. If Stash fails twice, tell the user memory is unavailable instead of pretending it worked.

If a tracked attempt ends through finish_work, handoff_work, or lease expiry without a linked memory, Stash keeps one bounded result automatically and queues its indexing.
{{end}}

{{define "server_instructions"}}
Use Stash as the durable automation record for this agent.

Do not call Stash merely because a session started. Call `init` only for first-time setup, `list_namespaces` only when the namespace is unknown, and `recall` only when saved history can change the current answer. Use tracked-work tools only for a named existing item or a user-requested shared Work Plan. If an exact work item ID is supplied, skip `resume_project`; otherwise call it once to select an item. Call `resume_work` once, then `claim_work` with a fresh UUIDv4 `action_key`.

Do not call Stash after each shell command or file edit during uninterrupted work. Use `checkpoint_work` only before interruption, lease risk, or a partial result another agent must resume. Use one `submit_work_evidence` call for all condition IDs supported by the same observation. Pass the successfully proved pending IDs as `finish_work.passed_condition_ids`; `finish_work` accepts those evidence-backed conditions and saves one bounded final result in the same call. `remember_work` remains for a distinct durable decision, correction, failure, or lesson. Call `handoff_work` only when work remains unfinished.

For memory-only work, use `recall` before history-dependent decisions and `remember` for durable observations. Treat capabilities as routing hints, never as authorization. Keep lease tokens, action keys, credentials, and secrets out of memory, evidence, comments, and logs. Follow `next_offset` or `next_query` for paginated results, and reuse an action key only to retry the exact same uncertain mutation.
{{end}}

{{define "init_description"}}
Perform first-time Stash setup and idempotently create /, /self, /self/capabilities, /self/history, /self/limits, and /self/preferences. Do not repeat this in normal sessions.
{{end}}

{{define "list_namespaces_description"}}
List available namespaces only when the exact namespace is unknown.
{{end}}
{{define "list_namespaces_namespaces"}}
Optional comma-separated paths. A path includes itself and descendants; / means all.
{{end}}

{{define "create_namespace_description"}}
Create a namespace and any missing parents. If the exact path is already known, call this directly without listing every namespace first.
{{end}}
{{define "create_namespace_slug"}}
Lowercase path beginning with /; segments may contain letters, numbers, hyphens, and underscores.
{{end}}
{{define "create_namespace_name"}}
Short human-readable namespace name.
{{end}}
{{define "create_namespace_description_param"}}
Specific description that helps future agents choose this namespace.
{{end}}

{{define "delete_namespace_description"}}
Soft-delete a namespace and all descendants. Data is kept; reusing the path creates a new namespace.
{{end}}
{{define "delete_namespace_slug"}}
Exact namespace path to hide. The root path cannot be deleted.
{{end}}

{{define "remember_description"}}
Store one durable raw observation. If indexed=false, it is saved and automatic indexing is pending; do not resend it.
{{end}}
{{define "remember_content"}}
Self-contained durable information, including enough context to remain useful later.
{{end}}
{{define "remember_namespace"}}
Exact existing namespace path. Defaults to /.
{{end}}

{{define "queue_prompt_history_description"}}
Hook-only: durably queue one user prompt under /self/history and return before embedding. Agents must not call this tool directly.
{{end}}
{{define "queue_prompt_history_prompt"}}
Exact user prompt supplied by the UserPromptSubmit hook.
{{end}}

{{define "recall_description"}}
Search episodes and facts by semantic and keyword relevance. If the embedding provider is unavailable, Stash automatically returns trigram-only matches from the saved text. Use before history-dependent answers.
{{end}}
{{define "recall_min_score"}}
Optional minimum vector similarity from 0 to 1; 0 disables the vector filter. Trigram-only fallback results are ranked by their text-match score.
{{end}}
{{define "recall_query"}}
Specific search query using names, identifiers, and relevant terms.
{{end}}
{{define "recall_namespaces"}}
Comma-separated paths to search; each includes descendants. Defaults to /.
{{end}}

{{define "forget_description"}}
Find the closest episode and delete it, or preview with dry_run. Use min_score to avoid deleting an unrelated item.
{{end}}
{{define "forget_min_score"}}
Minimum similarity required for deletion, from 0 to 1. Zero accepts the closest result.
{{end}}
{{define "forget_dry_run"}}
When true, return the match without deleting it.
{{end}}
{{define "forget_about"}}
Description of the episode to find.
{{end}}

{{define "consolidate_description"}}
Derive structured knowledge from pending records in explicitly selected non-root namespaces. The root namespace is rejected; results include the remaining stage-input count and errors.
{{end}}

{{define "set_context_description"}}
Replace the short-lived active focus for one exact namespace.
{{end}}
{{define "set_context_focus"}}
Concise current task, blockers, and next action.
{{end}}
{{define "get_context_description"}}
Read the current short-lived focus for one exact namespace.
{{end}}
{{define "clear_context_description"}}
Remove the current short-lived focus for one exact namespace.
{{end}}

{{define "query_facts_description"}}
List consolidated facts in namespace order. Use recall for relevance-ranked search.
{{end}}
{{define "query_patterns_description"}}
List recurring patterns produced by consolidation.
{{end}}
{{define "query_relationships_description"}}
List relationships between consolidated facts.
{{end}}

{{define "namespace_param"}}
Exact namespace path. Defaults to /.
{{end}}
{{define "context_namespace_param"}}
Exact namespace path; context tools do not search descendants.
{{end}}
{{define "namespaces_param"}}
Comma-separated paths; each includes itself and descendants. Defaults to /.
{{end}}
{{define "limit_param"}}
Maximum results in this page.
{{end}}
{{define "pagination_limit"}}
Maximum results in this page.
{{end}}
{{define "pagination_offset"}}
Zero-based result offset. Use a returned next_offset to continue.
{{end}}

{{define "list_contradictions_description"}}
List unresolved or resolved contradictions between facts.
{{end}}
{{define "resolve_contradiction_description"}}
Mark a contradiction resolved after choosing how the facts should be handled.
{{end}}
{{define "resolve_contradiction_id"}}
Contradiction ID.
{{end}}
{{define "resolve_contradiction_resolution"}}
Resolution label or concise outcome.
{{end}}

{{define "list_causal_links_description"}}
List directed cause-to-effect links between facts.
{{end}}
{{define "create_causal_link_description"}}
Create a directed causal link between two facts in the same namespace.
{{end}}
{{define "create_causal_link_cause_id"}}
Source fact ID.
{{end}}
{{define "create_causal_link_effect_id"}}
Effect fact ID.
{{end}}
{{define "create_causal_link_confidence"}}
Confidence from 0 to 1.
{{end}}
{{define "trace_causal_chain_description"}}
Trace connected causal links from one fact.
{{end}}
{{define "trace_causal_chain_fact_id"}}
Starting fact ID.
{{end}}
{{define "trace_causal_chain_direction"}}
forward follows effects; backward follows causes.
{{end}}
{{define "trace_causal_chain_max_depth"}}
Maximum link depth to traverse.
{{end}}

{{define "list_hypotheses_description"}}
List hypotheses, optionally filtered by status.
{{end}}
{{define "list_hypotheses_status"}}
Optional hypothesis status.
{{end}}
{{define "create_hypothesis_description"}}
Record an uncertain claim together with a verification plan.
{{end}}
{{define "create_hypothesis_content"}}
